  "body": "A checkbox has two positions. A settings file has **three** states: the key says `true`, the key says `false`, or the key is **absent** and Claude Code applies its own default.\n\nUnchecking a box wrote `false` — a different instruction from *\"I have no opinion\"*. For a setting whose default is `true`, that actively changes behaviour you only meant to stop overriding. And there was no way to say \"not set\" at all, so once a boolean was written it could never be taken back out from this page.\n\n## Now\n\n```\nsettings key    [ True ] [ False ] [ Not set ]\nenv variable    [  On  ] [  Off  ] [ Not set ]     writes \"1\" / \"0\" / removes\n```\n\nEvery state visible at once, one click to reach any of them. **\"Not set\"** carries a tooltip naming the default it hands back to, so it's an informed choice rather than a guess.\n\n**The presence-read family is the exception, with a reason.** Claude Code reads only *whether* `DISABLE_TELEMETRY` and its five siblings exist, so `false` isn't a state they can be in — those get `On | Not set`, and the row's `presence` badge already explains why. `FORCE_HYPERLINK` keeps all three, since it's parsed as a number and `0` genuinely is off.\n\n## A deliberate break with convention\n\nThe selected segment is a raised neutral surface with an **accent underline**, not accent-coloured text. Accent text is what the rest of this dashboard uses for a selected state, but at 12px on the light theme's raised surface it measures **3.4:1** — under the 4.5:1 floor. `--text-strong` on `--panel-strong` measures **16.9–19.8:1** across all four themes, and the underline carries the same meaning at any contrast.\n\nThe marker is a border rather than an inset shadow because **High Contrast sets `--shadow-sm` to `none`**, and `box-shadow: none, inset ...` is an invalid list — the whole declaration was dropped and that theme lost both the marker *and* the raised surface. Caught by measuring all four themes.\n\nThe segments are a real `radiogroup` labelled by the row's setting name, so it's keyboard-navigable and announced.\n\n## Verification\n\nLive server, throwaway home, port 8179:\n\n- **Six seeded cases read back correctly**: a settings boolean `true`, one explicitly `false`, one absent, a presence-read variable, an env `\"0\"`, and `FORCE_HYPERLINK`. `false` and absent are visibly different states — the whole point.\n- **Wrote all five transitions in one apply.** Diff read `true → removed`, `false → true`, `(not set) → false`, `1 → removed`, `0 → 1`. File on disk matched exactly: `verbose` gone, `autoCompactEnabled` explicitly `false`, `DISABLE_TELEMETRY` gone, `DEBUG` `\"1\"`, `FORCE_HYPERLINK` untouched.\n- Contrast in all four themes: **18.41 / 16.85 / 19.80 / 17.20**.\n- Segment heights identical selected and unselected — selecting shifts nothing.\n- **Two of my own measurements were wrong before the code was**: reading computed style right after a theme switch reads through an in-flight 150ms transition and returns the *previous* theme's colour; and a height comparison ran `Math.round` over a `\"32px\"` string, comparing `NaN` to `NaN`. Both re-measured with transitions disabled and with real numbers.\n- 5 new tests pinning that `false` and unset are different plans, that an env boolean writes `\"0\"` rather than being removed, and that a presence-read variable still can't be set false.\n- Full suite **3808 passed**, same 14 environment-baseline failures.\n\nDead `.cc-switch` CSS removed with the checkbox it styled.\n\nMINOR bump **5.11.0 → 5.12.0** — being able to unset a boolean is new capability.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TWCKNkSxNEfus8GfcqXnQD\n",
